 the Christian era) passed through Dila zawiya.” “It was only under Mawlây Rashïd that Morocco resumed its cultural traditions and its social and economic achievements. Mawlây Rashïd held scholars and men of letters in great esteem. He had himself studied at the Karâwiyyïn University. Mawlây Rashïd built the biggest madrasa (college) in Fez. This is the madrasa modeitly called Madrasa Cherratïn, from the name of the street in which it was built. He built another madrasa in Marrakesh.” “Muhammad b. ‘Abd Allah almost re-established order and restored to the town its past glory… It was he who made the 12,000 books of the library of Mawlay Ismail hubus for the benefit of all the mosques of Morocco.”'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1016, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 928})
